.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt AGY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm agy
.Nd Google's Antigravity CLI, a coding agent for the terminal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Fl p Ar prompt
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Ar subcommand
.Op Ar arguments
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a coding agent: in a full-screen session on the terminal it takes a
request, asks Google's models for the steps, and reads and edits files and
runs commands in the current directory to carry them out.
.Ql agy -p Ar prompt
runs one request without the screen and prints the answer.
.Ql agy --help
lists the options and subcommands, and
.Ql agy help Ar subcommand
describes one.
.Pp
The x86-64 GNU root has
.Nm
when it is built with the agents layer:
.Ql make ARCH=x86_64 GNU_AGENTS=agy os-real-gnu-ext2 ,
or
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=all ,
which the release to the installed machine uses.
The program is Google's own build of Antigravity CLI 1.4.0, a dynamically
linked Go program for glibc, installed unmodified as Google's installer
installs it, under the name
.Nm .
.Pa /opt/agy/bin/agy
is the program, and
.Pa /usr/bin/agy
and
.Pa /bin/agy
link to it.
Its use is governed by Google's terms, which
.Pa /opt/agy/TERMS
names.
.Ss Signing in over SSH
The first session that is not signed in shows a menu of ways to sign in:
Google OAuth, for a Google account, or a Google Cloud project.
With Google OAuth,
.Nm
prints the address of Google's sign-in page and waits for a code.
Open that address on any other computer, sign in there, and paste the code
the page then shows into the session.
.Pp
Instead, a key of the Gemini API is used without signing in, when
.Pa ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json
names the Gemini API as the model provider and the key is in the
environment variable
.Ev GEMINI_API_KEY :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{ "modelProvider": "gemini" }
.Ed
.Pp
.Nm
keeps the account's token in the Secret Service of the D-Bus session bus
where one answers, and otherwise in a file of its own.
Rach2 runs no Secret Service, so the token is in that file.
.Ql /logout
in a session removes it.
.Ss Updates and telemetry
.Nm
has an updater, which replaces the program with Google's newest release
in the background.
.Pa /etc/profile.d/agy.sh
sets
.Ev AGY_CLI_DISABLE_AUTO_UPDATE Ns =true
for every login shell, the setting Google documents to turn the updater
off, so the program stays the version the root installed; a new version
comes with a new build of the root.
The updater also stops where it cannot write the program's directory, as
an ordinary user cannot write
.Pa /opt/agy/bin .
.Pp
Each session of
.Nm
sends Google usage events, to
.Lk https://play.googleapis.com/log ,
and registers with
.Pa antigravity-unleash.goog ,
a server of feature flags, and asks it for the flags.
Google documents
.Ql enableTelemetry
set to false in
.Pa ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json
as the setting that turns metrics off, but this version writes the file
again without that member at each start, and sends the same events
whether it is false, true or absent.
Google documents no other setting that stops either.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev AGY_CLI_DISABLE_AUTO_UPDATE
.Ql true
turns the updater off.
.It Ev GEMINI_API_KEY
a key of the Gemini API, used when the settings name the Gemini API as the
model provider.
.It Ev GOOGLE_GEMINI_BASE_URL
the address of the Gemini API, for a server other than Google's.
.It Ev SSL_CERT_FILE
a file of certificate authorities to trust in place of those of
.Pa /etc/ssl/certs .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /opt/agy/bin/agy
the program
.It Pa /opt/agy/TERMS
the terms of its use
.It Pa /etc/profile.d/agy.sh
turns the updater off
.It Pa ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli
the settings, conversations, logs and cache, and the helper programs the
program writes there itself
.It Pa ~/.gemini/config
the projects and other settings
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Sign in in a session of
.Xr tmux 1 ,
then ask for a change in a repository:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ tmux
$ cd project
$ agy
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr tmux 1
.Pp
.Lk https://antigravity.google/docs/install?tab=cli "Installing and signing in"
.Lk https://antigravity.google/docs/cli/reference "The CLI reference"
